## 3. Why Those Numbers Happened â€” Same Period, Different Behavior

| Metric (daily avg unless noted) | A. Equal-weight | B. Honest 512 | C. Leaky 25k | D. This run |
|--------------------------------|---------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| **Final equity** | 150,471 | 151,187 | **157,138** | 141,251 |
| **Peak equity** | 170,923 | 169,877 | 168,430 | **172,854** |
| **Total return (2 yr)** | 50.47% | 51.19% | **57.14%** | 41.25% |
| **Annualized** | 23.17% | 23.54% | **25.84%** | 21.46% |
| **Mean net / day** | **0.0919%** | 0.0934% | **0.1025%** | 0.0852% |
| **Mean gross / day** | 0.0921% | 0.1033% | 0.1028% | 0.0860% |
| **Turnover / day** | **0.0022** | **0.0989** | **0.0022** | 0.0082 |
| **Trading cost / day** | 0.02 bps | 0.99 bps | 0.02 bps | 0.08 bps |
| **Max drawdown** | **12.47%** | 12.99% | **10.15%** | **22.44%** |
| **Daily vol** | 0.0076 | 0.0081 | 0.0090 | **0.0140** |
| **Sharpe proxy** | **1.93** | 1.82 | 1.81 | 0.96 |
| **Steps in holdout** | 459 | 459 | 459 | 459 |

**How to read it without jargon:**

*   **Turnover** = how much you shuffle. `0.002` = sit still. `0.099` = rewrite the portfolio every `10` days â†’ fees. `512`-step smoke churned the most; `25k` leaky learned to sit still; this run churned `4Ã—` baseline.
*   **Drawdown** = worst fall from a peak. `22.44%` for this run means at one point `172k â†’ 133k` before recovering to `141k`. Equal-weight only fell `12.47%`.
*   **Vol** = wobble per day. This run wobbled `1.85Ã—` the baseline â†’ risk penalties (the `reward = net -0.001*turnover -0.10*vol -0.20*drawdown` in `env.py`) ate the `net`.
*   **Sharpe** = return per wobble. `0.96` vs `1.93` baseline says the AI took more risk for less reward this time.

